#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54a3427a-3ed4-5605-9c49-74f759bcf245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54a3427a-3ed4-5605-9c49-74f759bcf245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288690} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fcd1929-8fa5-5e11-9699-492206e5fe2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6aaa3cde-2f29-5bb8-a80e-dee5f4f375ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-347169" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)-4{sin}^{2}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x))={sin}^{2}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5{sin}^{2}⁡(3x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(1-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3}(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{3}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{5\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{5}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{5\\pi }{2}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
